CC   -!- FUNCTION: Cysteine protease required for the proteolytic auto-cleavage
CC       between the non-structural proteins NS2 and NS3. The N-terminus of NS3
CC       is required for the function of NS2 protease (active region NS2-3).
CC       Promotes the initiation of viral particle assembly by mediating the
CC       interaction between structural and non-structural proteins.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00046133}.
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Induces a specific membrane alteration that serves as a
CC       scaffold for the virus replication complex. This membrane alteration
CC       gives rise to the so-called ER-derived membranous web that contains the
CC       replication complex. NS4B self-interaction contributes to its function
CC       in membranous web formation. Promotes host TRIF protein degradation in
CC       a CASP8-dependent manner thereby inhibiting host TLR3-mediated
CC       interferon signaling. Disrupts the interaction between STING and TBK1
CC       contributing to the inhibition of interferon signaling.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00046219}.
CC   -!- FUNCTION: RNA-dependent RNA polymerase that performs primer-template
CC       recognition and RNA synthesis during viral replication. Initiates RNA
CC       transcription/replication at a flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD),
CC       resulting in a 5'- FAD cap on viral RNAs. In this way, recognition of
CC       viral 5' RNA by host pattern recognition receptors can be bypassed,
CC       thereby evading activation of antiviral pathways.
CC       {ECO:0000256|ARBA:ARBA00046032}.
